    "rationale": "The 18 h aliquot diluted 10× read 0.1467 (×10 = 1.47). Diluted 20× it read 0.0737 (×20 = 1.47). The two dilutions agree with each other, and both are about 10% above the undiluted reading of 1.34. As a check, the 5 h aliquot diluted 10× read 0.0455 (×10 = 0.455), close to its undiluted reading of 0.424. So dilution scales correctly in the reader's low range. The flat level of about 1.34 from 7 to 18 h therefore looks like the reader saturating at high density. True late biomass is about OD 1.47, though the gap is modest."
